{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1398275-how-much-do-your-players-use-equipment-do-equipment-bonuses-make-things-too-easy","id":1398275,"title":"How much do your players use equipment? Do equipment bonuses make things too easy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-22T19:36:51-07:00","id":1398275,"title":"How much do your players use equipment? Do equipment bonuses make things too easy?","content":"Seems like for almost any Skill roll, there's a piece of equipment or two that could apply.<br /> <br /> Do your players make good use of equipment? I find most vampire coteries have at least one character with high resources so access to most equipment isn't too big a problem.<br /> <br /> Do you find equipment bonuses all over the place make rolls too easy? Or do you find the system is balanced around it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T23:58:55-07:00","id":1398294,"title":"","content":"I find the numbers work fine. Equipment is easy to get, sure, but that doesn't mean it's always easy to have when you need it; esp. higher end stuff. Though I don't allow equipment to stack (I feel that's how the rules are supposed to work, though I forget if it's spelled out explicitly or not). Having ten +5 pieces of equipment doesn't do you more than a +5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T05:28:42-07:00","id":1398335,"title":"","content":"This should have gone under general as it goes for any splat<br /> <br /> I Think The weaker someone is more apealing equipment will be.<br /> <br /> Thus Ghouls Dhampirs or Revenants first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T12:55:15-07:00","id":1398413,"title":"","content":"Equipment is nice to help out low dice pools, but they're appealing for high dice pools via exceptional success odds going up.<br /> <br /> I do think there's a valid perception that vampires use general equipment less than other splats, even if I feel it comes from lack of experience with the CofD idea of what equipment is.<br /> <br /> Some of it is that vampires don't have a magic item thing, where most splats have default and common (to them) way of bringing mundane equipment into supernatural arenas as more than just some bonus dice. This causes some people to feel that vampires aren't &quot;tool users&quot; in the same way as everyone else is.<br /> <br /> The other part is getting into the idea that lots of stuff that's not traditional gear in other games is equipment in the CofD. The idea of vampires being very presentation and fashion aware in their politics isn't just some sort of vanity. It cutthroat vampire politics the right outfit for the right moment is equipment to help them sway other vampires to their cause, or undercut another vampire's efforts. Being able to toss a few more dice than your opponent can easily bend things in your favor.<br /> <br /> When a coterie makes plans to disgrace an older entrenched vampire that's in the way of their ambitions, that plan is equipment as long as the group sticks to their plans closely enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T13:52:06-07:00","id":1398425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1398275-how-much-do-your-players-use-equipment-do-equipment-bonuses-make-things-too-easy?p=1398294#post1398294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the numbers work fine. Equipment is easy to get, sure, but that doesn't mean it's always easy to have when you need it; esp. higher end stuff. Though I don't allow equipment to stack (I feel that's how the rules are supposed to work, though I forget if it's spelled out explicitly or not). Having ten +5 pieces of equipment doesn't do you more than a +5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm fairly certain there is a rule that caps all modifiers at +5 and -5. Plus ultimately how would you use multiple +5 equipment on the same test anyways? You could use maybe one +5 equipment on a helping test that would then give its successes as dice bonuses to another test with it's own +5 equipment, but ultimately... <br /> <br /> I see Equipment as a way for players to overcome high negative modifiers. Like, the modifiers to crack a safe make it impossible, but with the right tools it becomes possible. And for players who add high skill on to high equipment, so long as that equipment is properly paid for and doesn't come with it's own legal difficulties, well, that's the point behind having high Resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T15:13:55-07:00","id":1398445,"title":"","content":"Over the course of the CofD there's been two versions of the +/- 5 cap: total or &quot;per source.&quot; The 1e core book even said to pick between those based on group preference and how much granularity makes sense for the scene. Over the years the books (esp. 2e move to each core book having the full rules in it and not always being 100% the same) haven't been as clear about that.<br /> <br /> Even so, &quot;equipment,&quot; is supposed to be one &quot;source&quot; as a whole, not each individual piece of equipment being one source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T17:12:42-07:00","id":1398467,"title":"","content":"I guess for me the thing that I find confusing is - some of the equipment seems to be flat out necessary to do the task, so that seems to feel like the task will always have an equipment bonus? Like, you can't very well use Computers for most things, so that means almost every Computers roll will have an equipment bonus. That feels kind of weird, but, then, I also never use negative modifiers and maybe those kinds of negative modifiers act in tandem with equipment so I shouldn't use one without using the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T20:17:48-07:00","id":1398514,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, if you need equipment to do something, having the most basic tools for the job is +0 or +1 maybe. Having a 5 year old basic computer isn't going to be a help (or hindrance) to online gaming, but you're probably going to regret trying to take on someone with a high spec gaming PC with a dedicated gaming desk and highspeed connection due to the big bonus for a major rig.<br /> <br /> And yes, the game very much expects the ST to be using negative modifiers a lot. That's the ST's primary way of imparting difficulty to a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T22:02:18-07:00","id":1398531,"title":"","content":"I've been running a ton of PbtA games lately so have very much fallen out of the habit of adjudicating difficulty. All this stuff used to come natural ten years ago, but not no more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T02:14:36-07:00","id":1398562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1398275-how-much-do-your-players-use-equipment-do-equipment-bonuses-make-things-too-easy?p=1398514#post1398514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, if you need equipment to do something, having the most basic tools for the job is +0 or +1 maybe. Having a 5 year old basic computer isn't going to be a help (or hindrance) to online gaming, but you're probably going to regret trying to take on someone with a high spec gaming PC with a dedicated gaming desk and highspeed connection due to the big bonus for a major rig.<br /> <br /> And yes, the game very much expects the ST to be using negative modifiers a lot. That's the ST's primary way of imparting difficulty to a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree. Final pool should be the mix of bonus and malus. Malus are given because of the difficulty of the action: including several factor.<br /> A simple example may be lockpicking a lock:<br /> Malus:<br /> - stressing situation: they are shooting at you (-2/-3), panicking (-1/-2 - it's even hard to use a common key when panicking), etc.<br /> - difficulty of the lock itself (-1 to -4/5)<br /> - etc.<br /> <br /> Bonus:<br /> <br /> - Having just paper clips (+0. It simply make the action possible)<br /> - Having a profesional lockpick (+2/3)<br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> As you see, having thenideal conditon and the right knowladge (skill), and plenty of time, I would not roll at all either. <br /> <br /> Worst situation you are escaping from a stalking monster, don't want to make noise letting your position to be spotted but you can hear its steps always closer to you, but fortubally you have a professional lockpicking tooo, then I'll go for a roll with some huge penality penalized by the environment, and lock difficulty, mitigated by the bonus coming from your equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}